okay let me think out loud for this one. I think I want to implement a search functionality here for the genres. I could add regex based search, but I am adding a simple search because I am learning right now. The plan is to first create an input element to take user input, and then run some blackbox function on it. This blackbox function would take in the user's query in real time, and have a dictionary or something to look things up, and would return the genres to the user based on the toLowerCase-ed query.
So the first step is to set up an HTML input element and design it according to my will. I might want to do this in a separate file, search.svelte so that I have everything separately for tidiness. 
Interesting, I am done with the input element and its styling. I was having an issue where w-full would make it acquire the entire screen's width, so I added an empty div around it with the right margin classes. I think it looks alright now. I have also added a border-emerald-500 on focus, I think it pairs well with the overall white+black+emerald thing I am going on, because I love Pokemon Emerald.
The next step is clearly drilling some bindings, I think that's what I will do later after taking a shower.
